'''''Survivor 49''''' is the forty-ninth season of the American competitive reality television series ''[[Survivor (American TV series)|Survivor]]''. It premiered on September 24, 2025,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://parade.com/tv/survivor-season-49-2025|title=When does Survivor 49 start?|work=Parade|last=Bloom|first=Mike|date=July 10, 2025|access-date=July 11, 2025}}</ref> on [[CBS]] in the [[United States]]. It was the seventeenth consecutive season to be filmed in the [[Mamanuca Islands]] in [[Fiji]]. The season ended on December 17, 2025, when Savannah Louie was voted the Sole Survivor, defeating Sophi Balerdi and Sage Ahrens-Nichols in a 5–2–1 vote.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ew.com/survivor-49-winner-revealed-final5-battle-finale-11869899|title=And the ''Survivor 49'' winner is…|work=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Ross|first=Dalton|date=December 17, 2025|access-date=May 24, 2026}}</ref> Louie became the fifth winner of Asian heritage, following [[Yul Kwon]] from ''[[Survivor: Cook Islands]]'', [[Natalie Anderson (television personality)|Natalie Anderson]] from ''[[Survivor: San Juan del Sur]]'', Erika Casupanan from ''[[Survivor 41]]'', and Rachel LaMont from ''[[Survivor 47]]''.

==Production==
On December 15, 2023, [[Manoa Kamikamica]], the Fijian [[Ministry of Commerce, Trade, Tourism and Transport (Fiji)|Minister of Commerce, Trade, Tourism and Transport]], announced that the [[Fijian Parliament]] had renewed its contract with ''Survivor'' for an additional two years.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.fbcnews.com.fj/news/fiji-secures-two-more-years-as-home-base-for-survivor/|title=Fiji secures two more years as home base for Survivor|work=[[FBC TV]]|last=Prakash|first=Praneeta|date=December 15, 2023|access-date=February 24, 2025}}</ref> A preview trailer for the season was released on May 21, 2025, right after the finale of ''[[Survivor 48]]'' aired. Like in the previous season, ''Survivor 49'' and ''[[The Amazing Race 38]]'' retain the 90-minute runtime; the premiere episode of ''Survivor 49'' ran for two hours.<ref>{{cite press release|title=CBS Unveils Fall Primetime Premiere Dates for the 2025-2026 Season |url=http://thefutoncritic.com/news/2025/07/11/cbs-unveils-fall-primetime-premiere-dates-for-the-2025-2026-season-333310/20250711cbs01/|publisher=[[CBS]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=July 11, 2025}}</ref>

The American broadcast of the finale was interrupted by an address by President [[Donald Trump]].<ref>{{cite press release |title=CBS News Will Air a Special Report for President Donald J. Trump's Live Primetime Address to the Nation from the White House, Wednesday, Dec. 17 at 9:00 PM, ET |date=December 16, 2025 |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2025/12/16/cbs-news-will-air-a-special-report-for-president-donald-j-trumps-live-primetime-address-to-the-nation-from-the-white-house-wednesday-dec-17-at-900-pm-et-689515/20251216cbs03/ |work=The Futon Critic |access-date=June 16, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=White |first1=Peter |title='Survivor' & 'The Floor' Season Finales To Be Interrupted By Live Donald Trump Address |url=https://deadline.com/2025/12/survivor-the-floor-season-finales-interrupted-trump-address-1236650737/ |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |access-date=June 16, 2026 |date=December 16, 2025 |archive-date=December 17, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251217005041/https://deadline.com/2025/12/survivor-the-floor-season-finales-interrupted-trump-address-1236650737/ |url-status=live}}</ref> The broadcast of the finale was not interrupted internationally, with the finale airing regularly in Canada, where the series airs on Global, and in Australia, where the finale aired on 9Go! as a special daytime airing alongside the intended American East Coast airing.

