== Reception ==
''Survivor 49'' received a mixed reception from both fans and critics. While the personalities of Savannah and Rizo, Savannah's winning gameplay, and the entertainment value of the post-merge section were praised, the gameplay of the other castaways as well as the edit and the pre-merge section were criticized. Many also felt that the "new era" format of the show had begun to feel repetitive and uninteresting.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Rawden|first=Mark|title=Survivor 49 Is Going To Get Way Better On Rewatch, And There’s An Obvious Reason Why|url=https://www.cinemablend.com/television/survivor-49-way-better-rewatch-obvious-reason-survivor-50|work=Cinema Blend|date=December 7, 2025|access-date=January 1, 2026}}</ref>

==Controversy==
During the pre-game sequester period at Ponderosa, two of the original cast members were caught colluding with each other. The situation became so severe, that they were ejected from the game before it even started; they were ultimately replaced by Jason Treul and MC Chukwujekwu, both alternates for this season.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/jeff-probst-explains-survivor-49-players-replaced-alternates-11794636 |title=Jeff Probst explains why 2 ''Survivor 49'' players were replaced by alternates |access-date=August 21, 2025 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |publisher=[[Dotdash Meredith]] |first=Dalton |last=Ross |date=August 21, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/survivor-49-alternates-reveal-thoughts-before-being-put-into-game-11798503 |title=The ''Survivor 49'' alternates reveal thoughts before being put into the game: 'I'm 100 percent ready to go in' |access-date=August 31, 2025 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |publisher=[[Dotdash Meredith]] |first=Dalton |last=Ross |date=August 28, 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250831095038/https://ew.com/survivor-49-alternates-reveal-thoughts-before-being-put-into-game-11798503 |archive-date=August 31, 2025}}</ref> Additionally, third place finisher Sage Ahrens-Nichols alleged that two other castaways, Jake Latimer and Sophi Balerdi, also engaged in pre-game scheming; these claims were corroborated by fellow castaway [[Annie Davis]] who was on the same starting tribe as Latimer and Balerdi.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Holmes|first=Martin|title=‘Survivor 49’ Finalist Accuses Several Cast Members of Pre-Gaming Before Her Season|url=https://www.tvinsider.com/1236531/survivor-49-finalist-sage-ahrens-nichols-accuses-cast-pregaming/|work=TV Insider|date=December 31, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Galante|first=Grace|title=Second ‘Survivor 49’ Castaway Accuses Co-Stars of Cheating|url=https://parade.com/news/second-survivor-49-castaway-annie-davis-accuses-co-stars-cheating|work=Parade|date=January 7, 2026}}</ref>

